From a8c36a8bf902757258f854667b16610f7c6bd43d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: artcashin <64659740+artcashin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 04:47:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] spark: force Chat Completions API for the
 OpenAI-compatible provider

llama.cpp's /v1/responses streaming emulation is not a byte-for-byte
match of OpenAI's Responses API: for reasoning-capable models (e.g.
qwen3-coder) it reissues the streamed text-part id between the
reasoning and answer segments, which ai v6's stream-text state machine
treats as a fatal "text part ... not found" error mid-stream. Bare
openai(id) in @ai-sdk/openai@3.0.49 defaults to the Responses API.

/v1/chat/completions streaming against the same model was verified
clean (proper role/content deltas, finish_reason: "stop"), so pin the
openai: provider to openai.chat(id) to force Chat Completions. Other
providers (openrouter, groq, ollama) are untouched.
---
 src/lib/providers.ts | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/providers.ts b/src/lib/providers.ts
index af4010c..5e5c610 100644
--- a/src/lib/providers.ts
+++ b/src/lib/providers.ts
@@ -36,7 +36,16 @@ if (openaiKey) {
       { id: "openai:gpt-4o", name: "OpenAI: GPT-4o" },
       { id: "openai:gpt-4o-mini", name: "OpenAI: GPT-4o Mini" },
     ],
-    resolve: (id) => openai(id),
+    // Force Chat Completions (`/v1/chat/completions`) rather than the
+    // default Responses API (`/v1/responses`, via bare `openai(id)`).
+    // llama.cpp serves both, but its Responses-API streaming emulation
+    // reissues text-part ids between reasoning/answer segments for
+    // reasoning-capable models (e.g. qwen3-coder), which ai v6's
+    // stream-text state machine treats as a fatal "text part ... not
+    // found" error mid-stream. Chat Completions streaming against
+    // llama.cpp was verified clean (proper role/content deltas and
+    // finish_reason: "stop"), so pin to it here.
+    resolve: (id) => openai.chat(id),
   });
 }
 
